    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the full test suite is green (34 passed, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed at creation per the formula: start at 1, +1 for a present email, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response field with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3), regenerated into `OwnerDto` at build time. This removes `membershipTier` from the response in favour of `membershipLevel`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Changed the mapping target from `membershipTier` to `membershipLevel`, computing `Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))`. The inputs (`email`, `namesakeCount`) are persisted, so GET returns the same level assigned at creation. The old GOLD-tier logic (driven by `householdMemberCount`) is gone.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (from the mapped DTO) instead of nothing tier-related, alongside the existing id/customerCode/registrationDate.\n\n4. **`AssignHouseholdMemberCount.java`** \u2014 Updated a stale doc comment that referenced the now-removed GOLD tier.\n\nVerified against the acceptance tests: Cp15 (level 3, no `membershipTier`), Cp23 (level 2, `membershipTier` absent), Cp24 (level 3 capped), and Cp21 (audit line records the level) \u2014 all pass, and the full suite of 34 tests is green.",
